  "body_mappings": [
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        498.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        597.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "One night in early 2016, after keepers at New Zealand's National Aquarium in Napier had left, an octopus named Inky crept through an aperture in the mesh atop its tank. The fugitive presumably dropped to the floor, crossed the room, and compressed its elastic body into a drain, whose pipe stretched some 50 metres to the Pacific."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        410.96141732283473,
        461.8976377952756,
        490.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "Staff reconstructed that route from the slime residue it deposited. Inky had resided in captivity since 2014, when a fisherman retrieved it from a crayfish pot off Napier. The breakout went unreported for about three months. Made public in April 2016, the story travelled the globe."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        323.26141732283475,
        461.8976377952756,
        402.46141732283473
      ],
      "text": "Such agility stems from an octopus's pliable body, which has no skeleton or shell. Its only hard part is its beak, so any crevice that accommodates the beak will do. Roughly two-thirds of its 500 million neurons lie in the limbs, which handle sensory input and react with some autonomy."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        215.76141732283475,
        461.8976377952756,
        314.76141732283475
      ],
      "text": "Its wits are as versatile as its anatomy. A giant Pacific octopus in Seattle learned to open screw-top jars, needing 15 minutes at the outset, later about two. In a 2010 study, octopuses came to discriminate between two strangers, a feeder and one who touched them with a bristly stick, adopting a different hue and posture for each."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        88.46141732283473,
        461.8976377952756,
        207.26141732283475
      ],
      "text": "In July 2012 the Cambridge Declaration on Consciousness listed octopuses among animals possessing the neurological substrates for conscious awareness. A November 2021 UK government review recommended treating them as sentient, and the Animal Welfare (Sentience) Act encompassed them in April 2022. None of this proves an inner life. Inky, somewhere beyond the pipe, remained wholly oblivious to the debate."
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        517.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        597.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "2016年初的一个夜晚，在新西兰内皮尔国家水族馆的饲养员离开之后，一只名叫Inky的章鱼从水箱顶部网罩上的一道开口悄悄爬了出去。这名逃犯想必落到了地上，穿过了房间，然后把它有弹性的身体挤进了一个排水口，排水口的管道延伸约50米，通到太平洋。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        429.1614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        509.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "工作人员根据它留下的黏液残迹，还原了这条路线。Inky从2014年起就一直居住在圈养环境中；那一年，一名渔民从内皮尔附近海域的一个捕龙虾的笼子里取出了它。这次越狱大约三个月都没有被报道。2016年4月被公开之后，这个故事传遍了全球。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        360.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        420.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "这样灵巧的身手源于章鱼柔韧的身体，这种身体没有骨骼，也没有外壳。它唯一坚硬的部位是喙，所以任何容得下喙的缝隙都行。它的5亿个神经元中，大约三分之二位于腕足里；腕足处理感官输入，并且在作出反应时有一定的自主性。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        272.1614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        352.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "它的机智/智慧和它的身体构造一样用途广泛。西雅图的一只巨型太平洋章鱼学会了打开螺旋盖的罐子，起初/最开始的时候需要15分钟，后来大约要两分钟。在2010年的一项研究中，章鱼逐渐能够区分两个陌生人，一个是喂食者，另一个用带刺毛的棍子碰它们；章鱼对每个人采用不同的颜色和姿态。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        163.66141732283472,
        461.8976377952756,
        263.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "2012年7月，《剑桥意识宣言》把章鱼列入了具备神经基质的动物之列，这种神经基质专门用来有意识的认识。2021年11月，英国政府的一份评估报告建议认定它们有感知力；而《动物福利（感知）法》于2022年4月把它们纳入了/包括其中。这些都不能证明（章鱼）有内心世界。Inky在管道另一头的某个地方，始终对这场争论全然不知。"
    }
  ],
